  "summary": "SDPD announced it will eliminate the generic 'other' category officers used to justify ALPR searches, after a City Council committee raised transparency and accuracy concerns and voted to draft an ordinance ending the city's Flock Safety contract. Councilmember Elo-Rivera cited nearly 4,000 'other'-reason searches this year, while Mayor Gloria opposed terminating the program.",
